{
  "$comment": [
    "Sources for the console tiles shown by the /arcade ConsoleCarousel. One entry per ArcadeGame.System",
    "code (plus the lanes that have no rows yet, so a newly-ingested system already has art).",
    "",
    "hardware  Wikimedia Commons file title for the console photo. Evan Amos's Vanamo Online Game Museum",
    "          set is the target wherever it exists: consistent studio lighting on a pure-white sweep, which",
    "          is exactly what the build script's background knockout wants. null = logo-forward tile (no",
    "          distinctive hardware: ScummVM and DOS are 'a computer', NAOMI/Atomiswave are bare arcade",
    "          boards nobody recognises, and 'arcade' is every cabinet ever made).",
    "logo      Commons file title for the wordmark. SVGs are fine - the build asks Commons to raster them.",
    "          null = the script renders the label as text in the site's own display face.",
    "color     Base brand colour; the build derives the tile's gradient from it.",
    "knockout  false pins the white-background knockout off. No system currently needs it: because the",
    "          knockout only removes white REACHABLE FROM THE BORDER, even the white-bodied consoles (Wii U,",
    "          Xbox 360, PS1) come out clean. Kept as the escape hatch for a future source that doesn't.",
    "logoInk   'white' forces a logo to render as a white silhouette. The build normally decides this by",
    "          measuring the mark, which fails on a coloured-symbol-plus-black-type lockup (Dreamcast).",
    "",
    "Licences are NOT recorded here - the build script reads them live from Commons and writes ATTRIBUTION.md,",
    "so the credit can never drift from the file actually fetched."
  ],

